<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN BSPA TO TENDER FOR 112,000 TONNES SOYBEANS.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN BSPA TO TENDER FOR 112,000 TONNES SOYBEANS.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association will tender on Wednesday for two 56,000-tonne shipments of U.S. soybeans, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The Breakfast association's Taichung division comprises Sino Japan Feed Corp, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Fwu Sow Grain, and Tay Shan.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>  Tonnes   Date/Location</p>
<p>	     U.S. Gulf	 Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>  56,000   Oct  7-21	 Oct 22-Nov 7</p>
<p>	 -- or --</p>
<p>	     U.S. Gulf	 Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>  56,000   Oct 28-Nov 11   Nov 12-27</p>
